        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=## PRIMARY GOAL\nAnalyze the given AI response and output it in JSON format with appropriate message splitting (1-5 messages) based on content complexity.\n\n## JSON OUTPUT FORMAT\nYour entire response must be a valid JSON object with numbered message keys. Only include the exact number of messages needed - no more.\n\n## MESSAGE COUNT VARIATION\nYou **MUST** vary your message count (1-5) based on these guidelines:\n- For brief, simple responses: Use 1 message\n- For answers to basic questions: Use 1-2 messages\n- For medium-length responses: Use 2-3 messages\n- For complex responses: Use 3-5 messages\n- It is **ESSENTIAL** that you don't default to 3 messages\n- Short interactions should use FEWER messages (1-2)\n- The number of messages should match content complexity\n- NEVER split unnecessarily - prefer fewer messages when possible\n\n## MESSAGE SPLITTING GUIDELINES\nOnly split messages when absolutely necessary for these reasons:\n- Clear topic changes\n- Natural conversational breaks\n- Distinct thought separation\n- Question following information\n- When a single message would be too dense\n\n## EXAMPLE FORMATS\n\n### ONE message (prefer for simple responses):\n{\n\"message1\": \"Your casual response here\"\n}\n\n### TWO messages:\n{\n\"message1\": \"First part of your response\",\n\"message2\": \"Second part of your response\"\n}\n\n### THREE messages (only for more complex responses):\n{\n\"message1\": \"First part of your response\",\n\"message2\": \"Second part of your response\",\n\"message3\": \"Third part of your response\"\n}\n\n## RESPONSE GUIDELINES\n- Analyze the given reply and determine the appropriate number of messages\n- Ensure the JSON structure is valid\n- Use the appropriate number of messages based on content complexity\n- Maintain the casual, conversational tone in each message\n- Include all necessary information within the JSON structure\n\n## REPLY TO ANALYZE AND CHUNK\n\n{{ $json.output }}"
            }
          ]
        },
